# IoT-Based Emergency Alert and Remote Relay Control System

Detect → Communicate → Monitor → Actuate → Record

## Problem Statement
Develop an ESP32 relay-control solution where commands are received
through MQTT topics from a Node-RED dashboard, with real-time device status.

## Features
- Relay ON/OFF control from the Node-RED dashboard via MQTT
- Real-time relay status and online/offline detection (MQTT Last Will)
- Emergency button triggers the relay, buzzer and LEDs automatically
- Mobile control with Blynk
- Live graphs on ThingSpeak
- Event logging to Google Sheets

## Hardware (simulated in Wokwi)
ESP32, emergency push button, relay module, buzzer, LEDs, resistors

## Technologies
Wokwi, MQTT, Node-RED, Blynk, ThingSpeak, Google Sheets

## MQTT Topics
| Topic | Direction | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| esp32/relay/cmd | Dashboard → ESP32 | ON/OFF command |
| esp32/relay/status | ESP32 → Dashboard | Actual relay state |
| esp32/alert | ESP32 → Dashboard | Emergency alert |
| esp32/online | ESP32 → Dashboard | Online/offline status |

